WEBVTT

00:00.440 --> 00:08.460
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but…</i>

00:15.160 --> 00:17.880
<i>It's all right</i>

00:17.880 --> 00:21.720
<i>Even alone, I'll be fine, but…</i>

00:21.720 --> 00:28.220
<i>You know, the truth is
 that no one is alone</i>

00:28.220 --> 00:34.800
<i>Things like happiness, 
loneliness, and even anxiety…</i>

00:34.800 --> 00:44.120
<i>We are born to savor all those things</i>

00:44.560 --> 00:47.770
<i>A single spoonful of sparkles</i>

00:47.770 --> 00:50.900
<i>Transforms everything into smiles</i>

00:51.180 --> 00:58.010
<i>That could be what I secretly wished for…</i>

00:58.010 --> 01:00.700
<i>That miracle</i>

01:00.950 --> 01:07.670
<i>We're each searching for
 our most precious treasures</i>

01:07.670 --> 01:13.960
<i>That's what our journey is for</i>

01:13.960 --> 01:21.090
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but...</i>

01:21.090 --> 01:29.320
<i>Each moment that passes before me
 shall be spun from hope</i>

01:43.880 --> 01:46.410
Hey, hey! Challe fenn Challe!

01:46.410 --> 01:50.400
Do you like it when a girl 
has her hair neatly tied back?

01:50.400 --> 01:52.870
Or do you like it when 
their hair isn't tied back?

01:54.950 --> 01:56.860
Hey, Challe fenn Challe!

01:56.860 --> 01:59.280
You can say anything! Just say something!

01:59.280 --> 02:00.170
You talk too much.

02:00.170 --> 02:04.300
What?! I said you could say anything, 
but I didn't mean <i>anything</i>!

02:04.300 --> 02:05.530
Give the question a serious answer!

02:05.530 --> 02:09.420
I have no obligation to give such 
a ridiculous question a serious answer.

02:09.420 --> 02:12.900
Look, you two! It's Lewiston! 
We haven't seen it in a while!

02:14.360 --> 02:17.370
It makes me remember 
what happened a year ago.

02:17.370 --> 02:20.320
I entered the Exhibition 
and we went to Philax...

02:21.360 --> 02:24.360
I saw Mama's spirit off on Pull Soul Day...

02:29.030 --> 02:30.730
What's wrong, Scarecrow?

02:30.730 --> 02:31.250
What?

02:31.830 --> 02:33.080
Do you have a fever or something?

02:33.080 --> 02:35.210
It's... It's nothing.

02:35.960 --> 02:38.860
<i>Challe is still calling me 
Scarecrow, as usual.</i>

02:38.860 --> 02:41.370
<i>He's a little kinder 
than he used to be, but...</i>

02:42.860 --> 02:43.680
<i>Still...</i>

02:44.730 --> 02:48.170
<i>Right now, the fact that 
he stays by my side is enough.</i>

02:50.500 --> 02:51.230
Oh!

02:54.620 --> 02:58.110
Where are you looking, 
making your horse walk that way? You dolt!

02:58.110 --> 02:58.960
Huh?

02:58.960 --> 02:59.530
Oh!

03:00.140 --> 03:01.160
Mister Kat...

03:01.160 --> 03:02.160
and Benjamin?

03:02.160 --> 03:05.710
Did you forget that I taught you 
not to call me "mister"?

03:05.710 --> 03:06.740
You birdbrain!

03:06.740 --> 03:08.600
I-I'm sorry.

03:08.600 --> 03:09.760
Honestly.

03:09.760 --> 03:13.000
We're reunited after a year, 
and this is how you say hello?

03:13.000 --> 03:14.460
Long time no see!

03:14.860 --> 03:19.390
Why is a cat who dislikes the cold 
wandering around Lewiston in the fall?

03:19.390 --> 03:21.200
Readying for your hibernation?

03:21.200 --> 03:22.090
Mister Kat?

03:22.090 --> 03:24.910
<i>Challe</i>! You little...

03:24.910 --> 03:28.600
But, really, why are you here in Lewiston?

03:28.600 --> 03:30.060
Do you have an errand here or something?

03:30.060 --> 03:33.340
What are you talking about? 
This year is special!

03:33.340 --> 03:36.150
If I didn't come now, I wouldn't be able 
to do business next year, would I?

03:36.760 --> 03:37.780
What?

03:38.610 --> 03:40.740
Could it be that you don't know?

03:40.740 --> 03:42.330
Know what?

03:43.950 --> 03:48.290
Honestly, what a bunch of petty tightwads.

03:48.680 --> 03:51.320
There's a place I go to 
all the time. Follow me.

03:52.510 --> 03:54.080
Oh! It's been a while, hasn't it?

03:54.640 --> 03:57.000
I never imagined that 
you all knew each other.

03:57.000 --> 03:59.560
Despite how I appear, 
I'm good at looking after people.

04:01.040 --> 04:04.180
So, what have you been 
doing this past year, miss?

04:04.680 --> 04:06.320
Is your work going well?

04:06.320 --> 04:07.010
Yes!

04:07.450 --> 04:09.470
After wintering in Lewiston,

04:09.470 --> 04:13.640
we went around visiting little towns 
and villages to sell sugar confections.

04:14.240 --> 04:17.000
Is that so? You've been working hard.

04:17.000 --> 04:19.470
Have you come back so that you 
can enter the Exhibition?

04:19.470 --> 04:20.490
Yes.

04:20.490 --> 04:22.160
Well, it is that time of year, isn't it?

04:22.160 --> 04:23.280
Proprietress!

04:23.280 --> 04:24.570
I'll be right there!

04:27.320 --> 04:28.530
Um, Kat.

04:28.890 --> 04:30.170
So, is this...

04:31.520 --> 04:35.450
Since last winter, you've gone 
around to a lot of places, right?

04:35.450 --> 04:38.320
You saw sugar apple trees 
along the way, didn't you?

04:38.320 --> 04:39.960
Did you notice anything?

04:43.480 --> 04:46.560
Everywhere we went, 
on every sugar apple tree we saw...

04:46.560 --> 04:48.740
the flowers had set poorly.

04:49.700 --> 04:53.180
I thought that the harvest this year 
would be a lot less than usual.

04:53.180 --> 04:54.170
That's right.

04:54.170 --> 04:58.110
This year, the sugar apple crop 
is unbelievably bad.

04:58.110 --> 05:02.440
If, as in average years, everyone harvested 
their own however they wanted to...

05:02.750 --> 05:05.150
it would likely lead to conflicts 
between factions.

05:05.710 --> 05:10.560
To try to avert potential chaos, that dimwitted 
reprobate came up with an agreement.

05:10.560 --> 05:11.470
Reprobate?

05:11.470 --> 05:12.840
Hugh Mercury!

05:12.840 --> 05:14.830
That dimwitted reprobate 
of a silver sugar viscount!

05:15.290 --> 05:17.640
Oh, that's right.

05:17.640 --> 05:19.340
So, what was the agreement?

05:20.030 --> 05:25.800
This year, the harvest and refinement of 
sugar apples by individuals is forbidden.

05:26.510 --> 05:28.180
Forbidden?

05:28.690 --> 05:32.160
This year, all of the sugar apples 
throughout the kingdom

05:32.160 --> 05:35.780
will be harvested in the name of 
the Silver Sugar Viscount, then refined.

05:36.220 --> 05:39.180
Only those sugar artisans 
who participate in the process

05:39.180 --> 05:43.240
will be allotted silver sugar commensurate 
with their labor. That's the edict.

05:43.240 --> 05:48.320
Then, to secure ourselves some 
silver sugar, we have to ask Hugh for it?

05:48.640 --> 05:50.890
It isn't that simple.

05:50.890 --> 05:54.540
He's the one who decided it, but the one 
who has a monopoly on this work...

05:55.560 --> 05:57.160
is the Radcliffe school.

05:58.860 --> 06:02.380
The Radcliffe workshops 
in every corner of the kingdom

06:02.380 --> 06:05.590
have already gathered up all the sugar 
apples harvested in their areas.

06:06.770 --> 06:08.730
Both the Paige school and Mercury school...

06:08.730 --> 06:11.910
are gathering in their workshops 
to help with the refining process.

06:12.330 --> 06:15.110
There is no other way to obtain silver sugar.

06:16.220 --> 06:19.770
But I hadn't heard anything about this.

06:19.770 --> 06:21.650
It seems you hadn't.

06:21.650 --> 06:25.960
That dimwitted reprobate's orders 
mean that even wanderers like us...

06:25.960 --> 06:29.800
should have been informed by 
artisans of the Radcliffe school.

06:30.270 --> 06:32.090
They deliberately failed 
to inform us, it seems.

06:33.280 --> 06:36.920
Everywhere she went, 
she was harassed by them.

06:36.920 --> 06:40.120
And it wasn't simply once or twice 
that they told her to get out of town.

06:41.460 --> 06:44.660
That's why I called them petty tightwads.

06:45.050 --> 06:48.490
Even I've heard rumors of the creator

06:48.490 --> 06:50.830
of the former Duke of Philax's 
sugar confection, one Anne Halford.

06:50.830 --> 06:52.390
It's no wonder some people are jealous.

06:53.050 --> 06:56.020
Basically, they're ostracizing you.

06:57.060 --> 07:02.480
Kat, if I want to enter the Sugar 
Confectionary Exhibition, what should I do?

07:02.480 --> 07:03.770
That's right!

07:03.770 --> 07:07.050
Participants need to have silver sugar 
they've refined themselves, right?

07:07.050 --> 07:09.640
They can't enter without it!

07:09.640 --> 07:12.450
So, they didn't tell you about 
that either? Of course not.

07:14.440 --> 07:16.640
Those who wish to enter the Exhibition

07:16.640 --> 07:20.540
must temporarily reside at 
the main Radcliffe workshop. It's the rule.

07:21.090 --> 07:23.360
There, they'll be allotted sugar apples.

07:23.360 --> 07:27.870
They'll refine silver sugar from them 
that they can use to make their pieces.

07:27.870 --> 07:32.120
But that's on the condition that they also 
assist in the joint refining process.

07:32.120 --> 07:33.600
There isn't time.

07:33.600 --> 07:37.230
That's right. The only time you'll have 
to work for yourself is at night.

07:37.230 --> 07:39.050
That's why everyone who wanted to enter

07:39.050 --> 07:42.190
arrived at the main workshop 
over two weeks ago.

07:42.730 --> 07:46.880
<i>This was going to be the year that I made 
a sugar confection worthy of the festivities...</i>

07:46.880 --> 07:49.510
<i>and became a Silver Sugar Master. But now...</i>

07:51.150 --> 07:55.120
<i>I can't let something like this stop me!</i>

07:56.580 --> 08:00.700
It appears that I must go to 
the main Radcliffe workshop.

08:01.570 --> 08:03.420
What do you think? Will both of you...

08:03.930 --> 08:05.200
will you come with me?

08:05.200 --> 08:08.670
Anne, if you're going, I'd follow you 
to the depths of the underworld!

08:09.410 --> 08:10.800
I will go with you.

08:10.800 --> 08:14.130
Leaving a fool on her own will 
never lead to anything good.

08:17.640 --> 08:19.100
Well, then. Let's go.

08:19.100 --> 08:20.500
I'll show you the way.

08:21.350 --> 08:23.210
But that's all.

08:23.210 --> 08:26.610
If you're an artisan, then prevail over 
whatever comes your way on your own.

08:28.840 --> 08:29.670
I will.

08:30.680 --> 08:32.610
Then I suppose we'll have you lead the way.

08:33.020 --> 08:33.840
Mister Kat.

08:33.840 --> 08:37.000
I told you! Stop calling me "Mister Cat"!

08:42.680 --> 08:46.420
All of the grounds within these walls 
belong to the main workshop?

08:46.420 --> 08:48.260
That's <i>incredible</i>!

08:50.680 --> 08:53.840
Then, if you'd just sign this 
on that desk over there.

08:53.840 --> 08:56.350
Hey. I'll be joining the work too.

08:56.350 --> 08:59.300
Oh. Of course. And your name is...

08:59.810 --> 09:01.340
A-Anne?

09:03.190 --> 09:04.380
Jonas.

09:04.380 --> 09:05.260
You know him?

09:05.260 --> 09:06.460
He's, well...

09:06.460 --> 09:07.350
Hey, Jonas!

09:09.290 --> 09:11.610
It's rude to keep people waiting!

09:11.610 --> 09:13.160
I'm so sorry.

09:13.160 --> 09:16.170
I'm the one in charge of 
reception here, Sammy Jones.

09:16.170 --> 09:20.450
You're Silver Sugar Master Alph Hingley, 
aren't you? I've heard of you.

09:20.960 --> 09:22.960
All I need is your signature here.

09:22.960 --> 09:25.020
I'll show you to your room.

09:25.020 --> 09:26.640
Don't worry about me.

09:26.640 --> 09:30.350
Deal with the person 
standing here behind me instead.

09:30.350 --> 09:32.130
And who are you?

09:32.610 --> 09:35.720
I've also come to participate 
in refining the silver sugar.

09:35.720 --> 09:39.320
And I intend to enter 
the Sugar Confectionary Exhibition.

09:39.320 --> 09:41.370
<i>What</i>? A woman entering?

09:41.370 --> 09:43.290
I know the type.

09:43.290 --> 09:45.180
People who can't make 
a decent sugar confection

09:45.180 --> 09:47.920
and still declare themselves sugar artisans.

09:47.920 --> 09:51.850
We couldn't possibly let a woman 
like that into the workshop.

09:51.850 --> 09:53.860
I am a sugar artisan.

09:53.860 --> 09:56.190
There is someone who has 
formally acknowledged my skills.

09:56.190 --> 09:58.450
Who? Your mom?

09:59.090 --> 10:01.160
The former Duke of Philax.

10:04.160 --> 10:07.680
You're Anne Halford? I've heard of you.

10:07.680 --> 10:10.790
They say you set Jonas up 
at the Exhibition last year.

10:10.790 --> 10:11.400
What?

10:11.400 --> 10:14.760
And on top of that, I've heard that you 
seduced the Silver Sugar Viscount.

10:15.100 --> 10:18.970
The Duke of Philax, too. 
Who knows what you did to earn his favor?

10:18.970 --> 10:19.630
What did you say?

10:19.630 --> 10:23.640
Well, regardless of who you may be, 
you won't be allowed inside.

10:23.640 --> 10:24.560
Why not?!

10:25.690 --> 10:27.680
You've got a companion fairy 
with you, don't you?

10:28.120 --> 10:30.650
Only people involved in the work

10:30.650 --> 10:33.650
and labor fairies are allowed 
in the workshop. That's the rule.

10:34.040 --> 10:35.480
If you want to work in this workshop,

10:35.480 --> 10:37.440
first go and sell that fairy!

10:37.440 --> 10:39.150
Challe isn't a companion fairy!

10:39.150 --> 10:39.990
It's the rules!

10:39.990 --> 10:41.690
Now, go away! Go on!

10:41.690 --> 10:44.120
Clean yourself up and come try again!

10:45.200 --> 10:47.830
That's enough unseemly behavior, Sammy.

10:49.030 --> 10:50.620
Kieth, I was only...

10:51.100 --> 10:53.820
You will tarnish the name 
of the Radcliffe Workshop.

10:55.640 --> 10:58.340
Please be quiet before I become displeased.

11:03.270 --> 11:04.550
Who are you?

11:18.070 --> 11:20.150
My associate spoke very rudely.

11:20.150 --> 11:21.590
Please forgive him.

11:24.080 --> 11:27.910
Kieth Powell, sugar artisan. 
Pleased to meet you.

11:29.480 --> 11:31.870
Oh! The pleasure is mine! I'm Anne Halford.

11:32.500 --> 11:34.030
Hey, Powell!

11:34.030 --> 11:36.380
I didn't know you were affiliated 
with the Radcliffe school.

11:36.840 --> 11:39.000
It's good to see you again, Mister Hingley.

11:39.740 --> 11:43.520
Kieth, this woman has 
a companion fairy with her.

11:43.520 --> 11:45.050
We can't allow them inside.

11:45.050 --> 11:45.960
Those are the rules.

11:45.960 --> 11:48.560
He isn't a companion fairy! 
He's a <i>warrior</i> fairy!

11:50.930 --> 11:52.020
This is...

11:52.660 --> 11:53.880
Amazing.

11:54.430 --> 11:57.450
I've never seen such a beautiful fairy.

12:00.080 --> 12:04.830
Say, Anne. You don't want 
to relinquish him, do you?

12:04.830 --> 12:07.880
He doesn't serve me.

12:07.880 --> 12:11.880
He's a dear friend. It's only that 
I don't want to be away from him.

12:12.410 --> 12:15.910
In that case, there is a way 
you can enter the workshop together.

12:17.240 --> 12:21.720
This year, I'm planning to enter 
the Sugar Confectionary Exhibition.

12:21.720 --> 12:24.550
I'd like to create a piece 
using him as my model.

12:26.150 --> 12:27.140
Your model?

12:27.420 --> 12:29.980
To that purpose, 
I'd like to borrow him when necessary.

12:30.460 --> 12:33.600
If you would consent to that, 
then he would be allowed to come in.

12:34.030 --> 12:37.040
Borrow? He isn't some 
belonging of mine, he's...

12:37.040 --> 12:39.020
That will work. Show us the papers.

12:39.020 --> 12:40.140
Challe?

12:40.140 --> 12:42.120
I will do this trivial thing.

12:43.180 --> 12:44.650
Do you want to be away from me?

13:00.200 --> 13:01.130
All right.

13:04.230 --> 13:07.680
This is where the artisans sleep.

13:07.680 --> 13:09.930
The regular artisans 
stay together in one large room.

13:09.930 --> 13:11.680
Private rooms are for silver sugar masters,

13:11.680 --> 13:17.310
or for those of an equivalent skill level, 
as determined by the master of the school.

13:18.500 --> 13:20.840
Anne, this will be your room.

13:20.840 --> 13:23.210
What? I have a private room, too?

13:23.210 --> 13:26.570
We can't allow a lady to sleep 
in the large room with everyone else.

13:29.620 --> 13:33.580
This is my room, so if you 
need anything, please let me know.

13:33.580 --> 13:35.460
A bed!

13:38.640 --> 13:39.540
What's wrong?

13:39.540 --> 13:42.000
I was thinking about how 
Kieth has a private room too.

13:42.000 --> 13:44.170
They must find his skills worthy of it.

13:44.170 --> 13:47.430
That Jonas is different though! 
In spite of how arrogant he is!

13:48.060 --> 13:50.990
And Kieth seems to be 
an acquaintance of Kat's, too.

13:50.990 --> 13:52.680
I wonder who he could be.

14:00.050 --> 14:01.610
Oh dear.

14:02.550 --> 14:04.190
You're a lot like a squirrel.

14:04.190 --> 14:07.150
A squirrel? That's so much 
cuter than a scarecrow!

14:07.480 --> 14:08.720
There's no calmness to you.

14:08.720 --> 14:11.720
You look exactly like a squirrel 
darting around looking for food.

14:12.240 --> 14:14.370
I <i>knew</i> it. That is what you meant.

14:14.940 --> 14:16.190
<i>My hair.</i>

14:16.190 --> 14:18.710
<i>Would I look more grown up if I left it down?</i>

14:19.130 --> 14:21.850
<i>I wonder which way Challe likes better.</i>

14:22.950 --> 14:25.270
Are you trying to break 
the mirror by force of will?

14:25.860 --> 14:29.090
I was only trying to see 
if my hair looked all right.

14:32.830 --> 14:35.020
It looks as it always does. No problems here.

14:38.480 --> 14:40.220
Say, Challe?

14:40.690 --> 14:43.690
Challe, would tied back hair be...

14:44.470 --> 14:45.480
Hair?

14:47.800 --> 14:49.570
It's nothing! Never mind!

14:49.960 --> 14:51.530
I'll be off now!

14:56.640 --> 14:59.580
I'm asking the same things 
as Mithril Lid Pod now.

15:00.190 --> 15:02.730
Starting today, I have to work 
as hard as I possibly can.

15:03.680 --> 15:04.840
All right!

15:09.810 --> 15:11.220
Anne. Good morning.

15:11.710 --> 15:15.120
Good morning, Kieth. 
Are you starting work now, too?

15:15.120 --> 15:16.920
I don't have a shift today.

15:16.920 --> 15:20.120
Once every seven days, 
we each receive a day off in turns.

15:20.120 --> 15:22.620
So, I was hoping to borrow Challe.

15:22.620 --> 15:26.400
Kieth, Challe can't be lent or borrowed.

15:26.780 --> 15:30.320
Oh, that's right. 
Challe is your dear friend, isn't he?

15:30.320 --> 15:32.140
I'm sorry. I phrased that poorly.

15:32.140 --> 15:35.440
It's all right. More importantly, 
I wanted to say thank you for yesterday.

15:35.440 --> 15:40.410
You really saved me. 
But why are you treating me so kindly?

15:40.410 --> 15:44.280
Anne, you are an artisan who has been 
acknowledged by the former Duke of Philax.

15:44.280 --> 15:46.710
I have no reason to be mean to you.

15:46.710 --> 15:47.630
Besides...

15:48.460 --> 15:51.010
our circumstances are a lot alike, you and I.

15:51.570 --> 15:52.870
Our circumstances?

15:53.630 --> 15:57.820
Anne, Emma Halford is your mother, isn't she?

15:57.820 --> 15:59.300
You've heard of her?

16:00.610 --> 16:05.510
When I was perhaps four or five 
years old, I met Madame Halford.

16:06.640 --> 16:10.700
I was surprised that a female 
silver sugar master existed.

16:13.000 --> 16:14.540
You met Mama?

16:16.630 --> 16:18.900
My father is Edward Powell.

16:19.500 --> 16:22.460
He's a silver sugar master, 
just like your mother.

16:22.730 --> 16:25.210
Edward Powell?

16:26.800 --> 16:28.630
The previous Silver Sugar Viscount?

16:29.040 --> 16:30.100
That's right.

16:30.540 --> 16:33.530
That's why I had many opportunities 
to meet silver sugar masters.

16:34.010 --> 16:35.880
It's also how I met Mister Hingley.

16:36.490 --> 16:38.200
My mother told me.

16:38.200 --> 16:42.340
He was a wonderful Silver Sugar Viscount 
who served for over twenty years.

16:43.030 --> 16:47.860
And if I remember rightly, about 
six months before Mama passed away...

16:47.860 --> 16:50.300
Yes. He died of an illness.

16:50.300 --> 16:53.650
But I don't know if he was wonderful or not.

16:54.170 --> 16:56.760
When my father was the Silver Sugar Viscount,

16:56.760 --> 17:00.410
there was a year like this one, 
where the sugar apple harvest was dismal.

17:00.990 --> 17:03.580
Apparently, it caused a lot of chaos.

17:03.580 --> 17:05.790
My father always regretted that.

17:05.790 --> 17:09.420
Your father came from 
the Paige school, didn't he?

17:09.420 --> 17:11.770
Why are you with the Radcliffe school?

17:11.770 --> 17:16.990
If I joined the Paige school, 
I'd get special treatment as Powell's son.

17:16.990 --> 17:18.550
I hated the idea of that.

17:19.130 --> 17:23.370
Here, I'd be treated as just another artisan.

17:23.370 --> 17:25.240
That's what I thought, at least.

17:25.240 --> 17:27.020
But it doesn't seem much different.

17:27.920 --> 17:32.040
I respected my father, but the situation 
was uncomfortably restrictive, too.

17:32.040 --> 17:36.060
And while my father was alive, 
I couldn't enter the Exhibition.

17:36.060 --> 17:37.260
Why not?

17:37.260 --> 17:41.870
Because if I received the Royal Medal, 
all those critics would gossip,

17:41.870 --> 17:44.110
saying that because I was 
the Silver Sugar Viscount's son,

17:44.110 --> 17:46.740
the royal family thought of me favorably.

17:47.160 --> 17:48.650
And if I didn't receive it,

17:48.650 --> 17:51.630
they'd gossip about me failing in spite of 
being the Silver Sugar Viscount's son.

17:51.630 --> 17:54.330
I couldn't participate for the sake of 
my father's reputation.

17:55.440 --> 17:58.430
But that ended last year.

17:58.430 --> 18:02.970
Now that the mourning period has ended, 
this year, I can enter the Exhibition.

18:05.340 --> 18:09.130
So, I was thinking of working 
on my piece today.

18:09.130 --> 18:10.360
Is Challe in your room?

18:10.360 --> 18:12.030
Oh. Yes.

18:12.030 --> 18:15.210
If you ask him, I think he will help you.

18:15.210 --> 18:16.410
All right.

18:16.410 --> 18:18.970
Well then, Anne, do your best out there.

18:21.270 --> 18:25.270
<i>Kieth isn't letting 
his circumstances stop him.</i>

18:26.080 --> 18:27.290
<i>I won't either.</i>

18:27.820 --> 18:29.120
<i>I can't let him beat me!</i>

18:35.190 --> 18:36.800
Sorry to ask this of you 
so early in the morning.

18:37.240 --> 18:40.300
I made a promise. I'll do anything.

18:40.300 --> 18:43.770
Shall I do a handstand? 
Or should I take my clothes off?

18:43.770 --> 18:46.240
State your orders quickly, boy.

18:46.240 --> 18:50.300
You and I don't appear 
all that different in age, but all right.

18:50.300 --> 18:54.010
If you'll stand by the window 
over there, that will be enough.

18:54.010 --> 18:56.860
I simply want to study your air 
and appearance, that's all.

18:58.180 --> 18:59.870
Things must be hard for Anne.

18:59.870 --> 19:03.700
The rest of us have already refined 
the silver sugar we need for the Exhibition.

19:04.320 --> 19:06.650
Since she's had a late start, 
she's only starting on it now, right?

19:06.650 --> 19:08.250
Thanks to the fact that

19:08.250 --> 19:11.720
your fellows didn't inform her 
of the unusual circumstances this year.

19:11.720 --> 19:12.670
Are you glad about that?

19:14.490 --> 19:16.130
They didn't tell her?

19:16.760 --> 19:18.900
Honestly, every single one of them...

19:19.360 --> 19:21.320
Such cowardly behavior is disgraceful.

19:21.800 --> 19:23.380
I hate it.

19:24.800 --> 19:28.470
But I'm glad that Anne is entering 
the Exhibition this year.

19:29.000 --> 19:33.860
The artisans gathered here 
won't be any competition for me, you see.

19:34.530 --> 19:38.160
There's a rumor that the Royal Medal 
will go to Sammy this year,

19:38.160 --> 19:40.900
but if you ask me, 
he isn't even worth a mention.

19:41.260 --> 19:45.870
Jonas is capable of creating good pieces, 
but he's missing a crucial element.

19:46.270 --> 19:49.310
If Anne is participating, 
then this feels more worth doing.

19:49.310 --> 19:51.820
You see, I've been wanting 
an opponent of equal skill.

19:52.400 --> 19:53.330
And...

19:54.770 --> 19:59.010
this will likely be the only year I get to
 compete with Anne in the Exhibition.

19:59.720 --> 20:04.010
I'm lucky enough to have been here 
for Anne's last chance.

20:05.010 --> 20:06.260
Last chance?

20:06.680 --> 20:07.740
That's right.

20:08.680 --> 20:11.750
If she doesn't become 
a silver sugar master this year...

20:12.660 --> 20:14.780
then she may not ever be able to.

20:17.310 --> 20:19.060
Anne drew too much attention to herself.

20:19.500 --> 20:21.550
With the events of last year's Exhibition,

20:21.550 --> 20:25.070
and those with the former Duke of Philax, 
she's become the object of much jealousy.

20:25.760 --> 20:30.190
If everyone were able to secure sugar 
apples themselves, as in an average year,

20:30.190 --> 20:32.660
Anne would have encountered 
some obstruction in obtaining them.

20:33.280 --> 20:35.860
That's why this was actually 
a stroke of good fortune.

20:35.860 --> 20:39.000
Because if she participates in the joint work, 
she'll be able to procure some.

20:40.130 --> 20:42.410
But things won't work out 
this way in the future.

20:42.970 --> 20:45.470
She'll never be able to obtain sugar apples.

20:46.610 --> 20:49.260
Please don't tell Anne about this.

20:50.330 --> 20:52.930
I don't want her to feel 
any additional pressure.

20:53.530 --> 20:55.600
I want to compete with her fairly.

20:59.080 --> 21:04.900
The Radcliffe Workshop

21:16.170 --> 21:20.500
<i>Is it just like the dreams we dream at night?</i>

21:21.370 --> 21:26.640
<i>Do we give names to our other dreams because,</i>

21:26.640 --> 21:30.180
<i>Just as our night dreams 
are forgotten upon waking,</i>

21:30.180 --> 21:37.250
<i>If they aren't held dear, 
they will disappear?</i>

21:37.250 --> 21:48.390
<i>No, it's because they aren't things 
that only special people can see</i>

21:48.390 --> 21:49.120
<i>That day</i>

21:49.120 --> 21:53.570
<i>I reached out again and again</i>

21:53.570 --> 21:59.130
<i>I failed to catch that shining fruit, and yet</i>

21:59.130 --> 22:04.630
<i>I'll reach out once more</i>

22:04.630 --> 22:08.930
<i>If I make my wishes come true myself</i>

22:08.930 --> 22:14.760
<i>I just know it will make you smile</i>

22:14.760 --> 22:26.240
<i>That's why I'm able to say I'm not giving up</i>

22:36.040 --> 22:39.960
<b>The Young Lady of the Paige Workshop</b>
